<title>FRANCE: Alcatel rises after Thomson offer.</title>
<headline>Alcatel rises after Thomson offer.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Alcatel Alsthom were firmly higher on Wednesday as the market digested the company's plans for Thomson SA.</p>
<p>At 1106 GMT, Alcatel was up 11.6 francs at 387 francs.</p>
<p>Financial analysts said the rise was partly due to the remarks by chairman Serge Tchuruk had helped but they also noted the share had been at historic lows recently.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a catch-up effect as the shares have lost 15 percent since it announced its intention to buy Thomson,&quot; an analysts said.</p>
<p>Analysts said Alcatel had presented a coherent project but added there were still uncertainties about the financing of the plan.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
